; `(cast T)` with its VALUE missing checked OK, and the emitter read the
; TYPE name as a variable: `%Int`, an undefined value llc refused
; (tests/fuzz/cast-missing-operand.axfuzz, found by the seeded fuzzer
; 2026-09-27). `isCastLike` keeps `cast` out of the saturation check,
; which is right for the SURPLUS it exempts - a cast's result is often
; a function value, and a further argument applies it - and left the
; shortfall unasked. It is AX3013 now, as a missing argument is
; everywhere else; AX3069 was already the surplus side for `sizeof`.
;
; A lone LITERAL after `cast` is AX3002's alone - "a literal is not a
; type", with the same `(cast Int e)` advice - and is not reported
; twice.
;
; An `.axbad`, like 395-sizeof-surplus: `format.ax` and the tree-sitter
; grammar both encode the form's arity and refuse this shape, and every
; `.ax` in the repository must parse and format.
(:: noValue Int)
(fn (noValue)
  (cast Int))

(:: literal Int)
(fn (literal)
  (cast 4))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (cast Int 1))
